0 Basidiocarps collybioid, rarely tricholomatoid; pileus convex, plano-convex to applanate or slightly concave, with or without  umbo or papilla, hygrophanous or not, translucently striate or not, dryor slightly viscid, glabrous or innately radially fibrillose;  lamellae free, emarginate or adnate, usually crowded, sometimes fairly distant, linear, segmentiform or ventricose with entire  or serrate edge; stipe central, cylindrical, sometimes broadened towards base, sometimes deeply rooting or arising from a  sclerotium, tough and firm, solid or fistulose; base usually strigose; spore print white, cream or pinkish.  ///Spores ellipsoid to oblong, ràrely subglobose to globose or lacrymoid, thin-walled, colourless, non-amyloid, rarely with  slightly thickened, dextrinoid wall; with confluent or well-delimitated hilar appendage; basidia 4-spored, clamped; cheilocystidia  usually present, cylindrical, flexuous, clavate or irregularly coralloid, thin-walled, never as broom-cells; pleurocystidia  absent or in a few species rare and inconspicuous; pileipellis a curis or ixocutis of radially orientated cylindrical hyphae, or  interwoven, more like a trichoderm, made up of irregular coralloid terminal elements ('Dryophila-structure'), never en-brosse;  hymenophoral trama regular to subregular; pileitrama irregular; clamp-connections present in aIl tissues. - ///Type species:  Collybia tuberosa (Bull.: Fr.) Kumm.///HABITAT & DISTRIBUTION - Solitary to gregarious, saprophytic on forest litter, deeply rooting on roots of trees, arising from a sclerotium or growing on necrotic fruitbodies  of other Mushrooms, in particular Russula species; widespread, cosmopolitan.025148375400
